{"meta":{"ui":"dashboard","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","form":"notation","designSystem":"cards","turn":"generate","prompt":"Show me how the product did this month as an inline dashboard with a toggle between 7, 30 and 90 days that changes every number. Four stat tiles with their change, each period: 7 days: revenue $18.4k (+4.1%), sign-ups 312 (+6.0%), churn 2.9% (-0.2%), active users 13,870 (+1.4%); 30 days: $78.9k (+8.5%), 1,340 (+11.2%), 3.1% (+0.4%), 14,260 (+6.3%); 90 days: $221k (+15.3%), 3,905 (+9.8%), 3.4% (-0.6%), 14,260 (+12.1%). A line chart of revenue over the period, and a bar chart of sign-ups by channel (Organic, Paid, Referral, Social, Email) that adds up to the sign-ups: 7 days 128, 84, 52, 31, 17; 30 days 540, 372, 218, 134, 76; 90 days 1,580, 1,010, 640, 420, 255. Under them a table of the top five plans I can sort by any column, starting with revenue, highest first: Pro 1,340 subs, $38,900, churn 2.1%; Team 412, $24,700, 1.4%; Starter 2,980, $8,900, 5.2%; Business 96, $4,800, 0.9%; Student 640, $1,600, 6.8%.","text":"Working through the notation: a period toggle as state, `let` values picked by period, StatTile grid, ChartCard for the line chart (revenue series per period, labels per period), BarChart for channels, and a sortable TableHeader/TableRow list with `sortBy`/`sortByDesc`.\n\nRevenue series and labels for line: 7 days and 30 days and 90 days need series of values; I'll use the period's totals spread as trend points, but the brief gives only totals, so the line chart uses the period's stated figures as its shape across the window.\n\nSort: table rows are in revenue order by default, with `sort` starting at \"revenue\" and `desc` true.\n\nstate period=\"30\"\nstate range=\"30 days\"\nstate sort=\"revenue\"\nstate desc=true\nstate tab=0\n\nlet revenue = period==\"7\" ? \"$18.4k\" : period==\"30\" ? \"$78.9k\" : \"$221k\"\nlet revDelta = period==\"7\" ? \"+4.1%\" : period==\"30\" ? \"+8.5%\" : \"+15.3%\"\nlet signups = period==\"7\" ? \"312\"